# Generated files are regenerated on a merge, never merged.
#
# Every path below is written by `make manifests`, `make generate`,
# `make helm-manifests` or `make ui-policy` from a source file in this tree.
# Merging two branches' *output* is the one case where a clean merge is worse
# than a conflict: git will happily interleave two deepcopy functions, or two
# CRD schemas, into a file that matches neither branch's input. Nothing says so
# at the time. It surfaces later as "the checked-in output differs from a fresh
# run" in CI, on a branch that did nothing wrong.
#
# hack/merge-generated.sh therefore resolves these to one side, and
# hack/regenerate-generated.sh rebuilds them from the merged sources — which is
# the only answer that is right by construction. It runs from hack/hooks/
# post-merge and hack/hooks/post-rewrite, because git reports a merge and a
# rebase through different hooks and catching up here is a rebase. `make hooks`
# installs all of it; without it these lines do nothing and git merges the
# files as text, exactly as it does today.
api/v1alpha1/zz_generated.deepcopy.go              merge=kitchen-generated
config/crd/bases/*.yaml                            merge=kitchen-generated
config/rbac/role.yaml                              merge=kitchen-generated
charts/kitchen/templates/crds.yaml                 merge=kitchen-generated
charts/kitchen/templates/manager-clusterrole.yaml  merge=kitchen-generated
ui/src/lib/policy.generated.ts                     merge=kitchen-generated
